    The schema every wiki example is generated from.

    This is a hand-written efrpg payload, not a captured one. It is deliberately tiny and deliberately
    boring: every example on every Settings.* wiki page is generated from these three tables, so a reader
    who has understood the schema once can read every page without re-learning it.

    It is NOT the wire-contract fixture. Generator.Tests.Unit/WireContract/EfrpgResult.xml exists to prove
    the tool and the template still agree about every attribute on the wire, so it is captured output and
    must stay captured. This one exists to be readable, so it is written by hand. Keep them apart: making
    this one "realistic" would make the pages unreadable, and making that one readable would stop it
    catching drift.

    The equivalent SQL Server DDL, which is what the wiki pages show the reader, is in DocSampleSchema.sql.
    Keep the two in step - DocSampleSchemaTests asserts the shape a page relies on is actually here.

    What each part is here to exercise:
      dbo.Category      a plain lookup table, and the principal end of a foreign key
      dbo.Product       identity PK, a SQL default, a computed column, a nullable and a non-nullable
                        string, a decimal with precision and scale, and the dependent end of the FK
      sales.Order       a table outside the default schema, for the schema-prepending settings
-->
